{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123797","id":4628011761,"node_id":"PR_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABE9na8Q","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123797","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123797.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123797.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123797","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123797/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/123797/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/123797/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/statuses/c574b57bdbe5b73b609b07263074caf5fb87532b","number":123797,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Expose window input handler","user":{"login":"kitbdev","id":10054226,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDU0MjI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10054226?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev","html_url":"https://github.com/kitbdev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\n- Effectively closes https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/15255\r\n\tSince a plugin can now be used for it.\r\n- Alternative to https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/123592\r\n\r\nExposes `Window::_window_input` as `handle_input`.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\n`DisplayServer.window_set_input_event_callback` was exposed which allows users to override the input that a window gets entirely. But it was not possible to only intercept the event and continue with regular input handling, because the default implementation is not exposed. Also if a user wants to stop overriding the input and go back to the default handler, they have to use a workaround like sending a mouse enter notification.\r\nThis is especially important for popups and other Window child classes that use `Window::_input_from_window`, which is not exposed.\r\n\r\n<details><summary>Touch Input Emulator plugin</summary>\r\n\r\n```gdscript\r\n@tool\r\nextends EditorPlugin\r\n\r\nvar stolen_windows := []\r\n\r\nfunc _enter_tree() -> void:\r\n\tvar root := get_tree().root\r\n\t_take_window_input(root)\r\n\tif not root.gui_embed_subwindows:\r\n\t\troot.mouse_exited.connect(_connect_to_window)\r\n\t\troot.focus_exited.connect(_connect_to_window)\r\n\r\nfunc _exit_tree() -> void:\r\n\t_return_all_window_input()\r\n\r\nfunc _connect_to_window() -> void:\r\n\tvar window_id := DisplayServer.window_get_active_popup()\r\n\tif window_id == DisplayServer.INVALID_WINDOW_ID:\r\n\t\twindow_id = DisplayServer.get_window_at_screen_position(DisplayServer.mouse_get_position())\r\n\tif window_id == DisplayServer.INVALID_WINDOW_ID or window_id == DisplayServer.MAIN_WINDOW_ID:\r\n\t\treturn\r\n\r\n\tvar win_obj_id := DisplayServer.window_get_attached_instance_id(window_id)\r\n\tvar window := instance_from_id(win_obj_id) as Window\r\n\tif window == null:\r\n\t\tprinterr(\"Failed to connect to window \", window_id)\r\n\t\treturn\r\n\r\n\tif not window.mouse_exited.is_connected(_connect_to_window):\r\n\t\t# Window focus exited isn't emitted for popups so also connect to mouse exit.\r\n\t\twindow.mouse_exited.connect(_connect_to_window)\r\n\t\twindow.focus_exited.connect(_connect_to_window)\r\n\t_take_window_input(window)\r\n\r\nfunc _take_window_input(window: Window)-> void:\r\n\tvar win_obj_id := window.get_instance_id()\r\n\tif stolen_windows.has(win_obj_id):\r\n\t\treturn\r\n\tvar window_id := window.get_window_id()\r\n\tif window_id == DisplayServer.INVALID_WINDOW_ID:\r\n\t\tprinterr(\"Window `%s` is invalid\" % window.name)\r\n\t\treturn\r\n\r\n\t#print(\"Taking window input for window `%s`\" % window.name)\r\n\tstolen_windows.push_back(win_obj_id)\r\n\tDisplayServer.window_set_input_event_callback(_window_input.bind(window_id), window_id)\r\n\twindow.tree_exited.connect(_window_exited.bind(window))\r\n\twindow.visibility_changed.connect(_window_exited.bind(window))\r\n\r\nfunc _window_exited(window: Window) -> void:\r\n\tif window.visible and window.is_inside_tree():\r\n\t\treturn\r\n\t#print(\"Window `%s` exited\" % [window.name])\r\n\t_return_window_input(window)\r\n\r\nfunc _return_window_input(window: Window)-> void:\r\n\twindow.tree_exited.disconnect(_window_exited)\r\n\twindow.visibility_changed.disconnect(_window_exited)\r\n\t\r\n\tvar win_obj_id := window.get_instance_id()\r\n\tstolen_windows.erase(win_obj_id)\r\n\r\n\tvar window_id := window.get_window_id()\r\n\t#print(\"Returning input to window %s `%s`\" %[window_id, window.name])\r\n\tif window_id == DisplayServer.INVALID_WINDOW_ID:\r\n\t\t#printerr(\"Window `%s` is invalid\" % window.name)\r\n\t\treturn\r\n\tDisplayServer.window_set_input_event_callback(window.handle_input, window_id)\r\n\r\nfunc _return_all_window_input() -> void:\r\n\t#print(\"Returning window input\")\r\n\tvar all_stolen := stolen_windows.duplicate()\r\n\tfor win_obj_id in all_stolen:\r\n\t\tvar window := instance_from_id(win_obj_id) as Window\r\n\t\tif window == null:\r\n\t\t\tprinterr(\"Failed to get to window \", win_obj_id)\r\n\t\t\tcontinue\r\n\t\t_return_window_input(window)\r\n\t\r\n\tstolen_windows.clear()\r\n\r\nfunc _window_input(event: InputEvent, window_id: int) -> void:\r\n\tif not DisplayServer.get_window_list().has(window_id):\r\n\t\tprinterr(\"_window_input Nonexistent window %s\" % window_id)\r\n\t\treturn\r\n\tvar win_obj_id := DisplayServer.window_get_attached_instance_id(window_id)\r\n\tvar window := instance_from_id(win_obj_id) as Window\r\n\tif window == null:\r\n\t\tprinterr(\"_window_input Failed to get to window \", window_id)\r\n\t\treturn\r\n\t\r\n\t#print(\"stole input from window %s : %s\" % [window_id, event])\r\n\t\r\n\tif event.device == InputEvent.DEVICE_ID_EMULATION:\r\n\t\treturn\r\n\r\n\tvar pan_multiplier := 15\r\n\tvar mb := event as InputEventMouseButton\r\n\tif mb:\r\n\t\tvar vertical_wheel = mb.button_index == MOUSE_BUTTON_WHEEL_UP or mb.button_index == MOUSE_BUTTON_WHEEL_DOWN\r\n\t\tvar horizontal_wheel = mb.button_index == MOUSE_BUTTON_WHEEL_LEFT or mb.button_index == MOUSE_BUTTON_WHEEL_RIGHT\r\n\t\tif vertical_wheel or horizontal_wheel:\r\n\t\t\tvar pan_event := InputEventPanGesture.new()\r\n\t\t\tpan_event.position = mb.position\r\n\t\t\tif vertical_wheel:\r\n\t\t\t\tvar flip := -1 if mb.button_index == MOUSE_BUTTON_WHEEL_UP else 1\r\n\t\t\t\tpan_event.delta = Vector2(0, mb.factor * flip) * pan_multiplier\r\n\t\t\telse:\r\n\t\t\t\tvar flip := -1 if mb.button_index == MOUSE_BUTTON_WHEEL_LEFT else 1\r\n\t\t\t\tpan_event.delta = Vector2(mb.factor * flip, 0) * pan_multiplier\r\n\t\t\tpan_event.window_id = mb.window_id\r\n\t\t\t_send_input_to_window(pan_event, window)\r\n\t\t\treturn\r\n\r\n\t\t# emulate mouse from touch\r\n\t\t# the setting won't work as we already missed where it applies in Input, so do it manually\r\n\t\tvar emulated_event := event.duplicate()\r\n\t\temulated_event.device = InputEvent.DEVICE_ID_EMULATION\r\n\t\t_send_input_to_window(emulated_event, window)\r\n\r\n\t\tif mb.button_index == MOUSE_BUTTON_LEFT or mb.button_index == MOUSE_BUTTON_RIGHT:\r\n\t\t\tvar touch_event := InputEventScreenTouch.new()\r\n\t\t\ttouch_event.pressed = mb.pressed\r\n\t\t\ttouch_event.canceled = mb.canceled\r\n\t\t\ttouch_event.position = mb.position\r\n\t\t\ttouch_event.double_tap = mb.double_click\r\n\t\t\ttouch_event.long_press = mb.button_index == MOUSE_BUTTON_RIGHT\r\n\t\t\ttouch_event.window_id = mb.window_id\r\n\t\t\t_send_input_to_window(touch_event, window)\r\n\t\treturn\r\n\t\r\n\tvar mm := event as InputEventMouseMotion\r\n\tif mm:\r\n\t\tif mm.button_mask & MOUSE_BUTTON_MASK_MIDDLE:\r\n\t\t\tvar pan_event := InputEventPanGesture.new()\r\n\t\t\tpan_event.position = mm.position\r\n\t\t\tpan_event.delta = -mm.relative\r\n\t\t\tpan_event.window_id = mm.window_id\r\n\t\t\t_send_input_to_window(pan_event, window)\r\n\t\t\treturn\r\n\t\t\r\n\r\n\t\tif mm.button_mask & MOUSE_BUTTON_MASK_LEFT or mm.button_mask & MOUSE_BUTTON_MASK_RIGHT:\r\n\t\t\t# emulate mouse from touch\r\n\t\t\tvar emulated_event := event.duplicate()\r\n\t\t\temulated_event.device = InputEvent.DEVICE_ID_EMULATION\r\n\t\t\t_send_input_to_window(emulated_event, window)\r\n\t\t\r\n\t\t\tvar drag_event := InputEventScreenDrag.new()\r\n\t\t\tdrag_event.position = mm.global_position\r\n\t\t\tdrag_event.relative = mm.relative\r\n\t\t\tdrag_event.screen_relative = mm.screen_relative\r\n\t\t\tdrag_event.tilt = mm.tilt\r\n\t\t\tdrag_event.pen_inverted = mm.pen_inverted\r\n\t\t\tdrag_event.pressure = mm.pressure\r\n\t\t\tdrag_event.velocity = mm.velocity\r\n\t\t\tdrag_event.screen_velocity = mm.screen_velocity\r\n\t\t\tdrag_event.window_id = mm.window_id\r\n\t\t\t_send_input_to_window(drag_event, window)\r\n\t\treturn\r\n\t\r\n\t_send_input_to_window(event, window)\r\n\r\nfunc _send_input_to_window(event: InputEvent, window: Window) -> void:\r\n\t#print(\"Sending to `%s` %s\" % [window.name, event])\r\n\twindow.handle_input(event)\r\n\r\n```\r\n\r\n</details> ","labels":[{"id":73330066,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw3MzMzMDA2Ng==","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/enhancement","name":"enhancement","description":"","color":"aaccff","default":true,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":890310664,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw4OTAzMTA2NjQ=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:input","name":"topic:input","description":"","color":"ffee88","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":{"id":8237783,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4AfbLX","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/16","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/16/labels","number":16,"state":"open","title":"4.x","description":"Issues and pull requests slated for an undetermined Godot 4 release.","creator":{"login":"akien-mga","id":4701338,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3MDEzMzg=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4701338?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga","html_url":"https://github.com/akien-mga","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akien-mga/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":5790,"closed_issues":0,"created_at":"2022-07-26T12:42:05Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T08:16:48Z","closed_at":null,"due_on":null},"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-09-24T15:48:45Z","updated_at":"2026-10-08T21:35:51Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"d033eb3ded170117ae9f459